    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Flynn are delighted to present an excellent opportunity to acquire this well presented two bedroom terraced house in the highly sought-after development of Manorfields.\n\nThis deceptively spacious property extends to approximately 70 sq.m (753 sq.ft) and is thoughtfully laid out to maximise space and natural light throughout. \n\nThe ground floor accommodation comprises an entrance hallway leading to a spacious lounge and fitted kitchen/diner, creating a bright and welcoming living space with sliding doors providing direct access to the rear garden.\n\nUpstairs, the property features two generously sized bedrooms and a main family bathroom.\n\n Ideally positioned, the property enjoys a private, well maintained and light filled rear garden, along with a driveway providing off-street parking.\n\nThe home has been well maintained by its current owners and comes to the market in excellent condition throughout, offering significant potential for any discerning purchaser.\n\n All in all, this is a spacious & superbly presented property - just oozing potential this is a perfect starter home or investment opportunity alike.\n\nSuperbly located in this mature & much sought after area of Clonee with an abundance of amenities closeby including local shops, primary / secondary schools, recreational parks, sporting facilities & an excellent public transport service linking Dublin City Centre in 25 minutes door to door. A short distance to the Villages of Clonee, Ongar & Blanchardstown Blanchardstown Shopping Centre, Hansfield Train Station, the Dublin 15 Corporate Parks, the Phoenix Park, the National Aquatic Centre, the N3 / M50 Motorways & Dublin International Airport. \n\nEarly viewing is advised."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway - 1.31m (4'4\") x 1.03m (3'5\")\nwith solid wood floor, alarm panel & ceiling coving.\n\nLounge - 5.84m (19'2\") x 3.72m (12'2\")\nwith solid wood floor, ceiling coving, feature fireplace with timber surround, slate hearth & electric fire inset. Understair storage.\n\nKitchen / Diner\nwith a range of floor & eye level fitted press units with tiled splashback. Integrated oven, electric hob & extractor fan. Tiled flor & sliding door to rear garden.\n\nLanding - 1.92m (6'4\") x 1.05m (3'5\")\nwith carpet & access to attic via pull down ladder.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.71m (12'2\") x 3.77m (12'4\")\nto front of house with carpet & built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.93m (9'7\") x 3.73m (12'3\")\nto rear of house with carpet & built in wardrobes.\n\nMain Bathroom - 2.58m (8'6\") x 1.61m (5'3\")\nwith w.c., w.h.b., & shower attachment cubicle & electric shower. Fully tiled.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Gas Fired Central Heating </li><li> Double Glazed uPVC Windows </li><li> Off Street Parking to Front </li><li> South West Facing Rear Garden </li><li> Built 2000 - 70sqm approx.</li></ul>"
